{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1387212-jaggling-avatars","id":1387212,"title":"jaggling avatars","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-10T02:07:01-07:00","id":1387212,"title":"jaggling avatars","content":"What happens to jaggling avatars who are pack totems when the pack finally ends (all members leave or are dead)? Do they just become ordinary jagglings? Wander off? Do they get reabsorbed by the Incarna? Something else?<br /> <br /> Since both jaggling avatars and jagglings are spawned be their Incarna, what is the actual difference between them besides the name?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T21:33:42-07:00","id":1387409,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if there's a canon answer but I would imagine it comes down to whether or not the spirit is recalled by the Incarna or cast out into the umbral wilderness to seek a niche or to find another pack. <br /> <br /> If they had been working with the pack for any amount of time they've probably gotten a fairly significant bolster to their own gnosis thanks to the service and offerings received from the pack. Even without that steady income, they've got reason to swagger more then the average jaggling.<br /> <br /> Generally the avatar spirit serves as a vessel for incarna, a representative of the greater whole. However these avatars have been known to take on unique personalities if given opportunity of time and gnosis, slowly becoming distinct from the formal avatar. The most famous case of this iirc was how one martial pack following 'Rat' slowly transformed their pack totem into 'War Rat', a distinct face of the greater Rat totem.<br /> <br /> So really what it comes down to is that these spirits have their place in the umbral hierarchies and are defined by their natural gnosis like any other spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T07:49:55-07:00","id":1387493,"title":"","content":"Can't think of a canon answer either.<br /> <br /> I would agree with the assessment above, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T08:10:10-07:00","id":1387496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1387212-jaggling-avatars#post1387212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens to jaggling avatars who are pack totems when the pack finally ends (all members leave or are dead)? Do they just become ordinary jagglings? Wander off? Do they get reabsorbed by the Incarna? Something else?<br /> <br /> Since both jaggling avatars and jagglings are spawned be their Incarna, what is the actual difference between them besides the name?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been asking this question for years. The books don't address it and conservatively they probably assume the that once the packs members contributing to the totem die or retire the spirit is depowered. But I like the idea that Pack Totems keep the power as a sacrifice when the pack dies, though they are probably a bit weaker without the pack.<br /> <br /> But honestly if the setting wasn't part of a game you would likely have multigeneration packs where new Garou join the packs already existing from their parents or cousins.<br /> <br /> <br /> Another thing not discussed is what ritual do you perform when you add members to the pack, the totem ritual after all is just for founding a pack, and its trappings are preparation for a hunt, not anointing someone to join an existing spirits patronage.<br /> <br /> I was always fond of Totem avatars of Caerns and packs being a living ecosystem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T15:10:28-07:00","id":1387604,"title":"","content":"Since this seems to be an open issue with no canonical answer, I think I'll rule that it depends on the jaggling avatar. Many are re-asborbed back into the Incarna when they are done. However, some pack totems that were particularly noteworthy or beloved by their packs and developed individual personalities as a result, were allowed to continue to exist although they lose their avatar status. They might have larger Essence than normal, but would lose a lot of the additional powers they had as a result of the Totem background. Some of these spirits are &quot;earmarked&quot; to become future caern spirits should new caerns (or rediscovered lost ones) be created.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1387212-jaggling-avatars?p=1387496#post1387496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But honestly if the setting wasn't part of a game you would likely have multigeneration packs where new Garou join the packs already existing from their parents or cousins.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually something that I do have for NPCs in my games. Most packs are new, but some &quot;leadership&quot; packs at septs are old with old members dying or retiring, and new ones being recruited as they become leaders of that sept. And some packs are exceptionally illustrious and have pack quests that are particularly ongoing. Of course, such pack totems have their powers eb and flow as the cumulative Totem points of its members fluctuate. When a pack member leaves, he takes his totem points away. I typically rule that any powers not properly accounted for are gradually lost over time, typically a few months.<br /> <br /> I don't have any firm guidelines as to how frequent multigenerational packs are. I just determine them if I think it makes an interesting setting/story element. But I suspect it'd be around 10-20% total. But most multi-generational packs last a few decades or century at most. Although a few packs might last for centuries. maybe even a thousand years.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1387212-jaggling-avatars?p=1387496#post1387496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing not discussed is what ritual do you perform when you add members to the pack, the totem ritual after all is just for founding a pack, and its trappings are preparation for a hunt, not anointing someone to join an existing spirits patronage.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my chronicies, I say that it is a variant of the Rite of the Totem. New members still have to quest to be accepted by the Totem. (Although for PCs, this is handwaved and the quest is collaborated as a prelude.) Mechanically it is the exact same rite. Any variation in the rite is accounted for by the ritemaster rolling his Rituals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 05-11-2020, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}